# Answering a question in your own words, and putting one away: ANSWERS=scripts/duo-markdown.json HEX=kept scripts/duo tap <ref> scripts/duo-ask-taps
# Words typed on its card and not sent stay there: the page closes, and the app starts again, and
# the card opens on them, the keyboard down.
launch hexvoice:///?tasks=md
wait 3
tap ask-card
wait 1
tap Write your own
type ask-input Found one of them
above-keyboard ask-input
above-keyboard Answer
shoot ask-writing
tap task-back
wait 1
no-keyboard leaving the page
open hexvoice:///?tasks=md
wait 2
shoot ask-held
launch hexvoice:///?tasks=md
wait 3
no-keyboard opening on held words
shoot ask-held-relaunch
# A swipe left puts it away, as in Mail: its row folds to Not needed, with Undo.
swipe-left ask-card
wait 1
shoot ask-swiped
tap xmark
wait 1
shoot ask-put-away
tap Undo
wait 1
shoot ask-back
# Swiped away while typing, it lets go of the keyboard and the page's foot comes back.
type ask-input  still
swipe-left ask-card
wait 1
tap xmark
wait 1
no-keyboard after a swipe while typing
frame thread-write
tap Undo
wait 1
# The same swipe on its row in the Tasks list.
launch hexvoice:///?tasks
wait 3
tap tasks-search
type tasks-search-field EDD
swipe-left markdown asks
wait 1
shoot row-swiped
tap xmark
wait 1
shoot row-put-away
# The button tapped says where the words go: a note, from the foot while typing, leaves the
# question open and says so; an answer, from the field's box with the keyboard down, folds it to
# what was said. Either way the page's own foot comes back.
launch hexvoice:///?tasks=md
wait 3
tap ask-input
above-keyboard ask-input
above-keyboard Answer
shoot ask-typing-held
tap Send as note
wait 1
no-keyboard after the note
frame thread-write
shoot ask-noted
tap Write your own
type ask-input Found both
swipe-down ask-input
wait 1
no-keyboard before answering
shoot ask-to-answer
tap Answer
wait 1
frame thread-write
shoot ask-answered
